    <solution><me>\mathbf{r}'(t)=\langle 4,-4,2\rangle</me>
and so
<me>||\mathbf{r}'(t)||=\sqrt{4^2+(-4)^2+2^2}=\sqrt{36}.</me>
The unit tangent vector is therefore:
<me>\mathbf{T}(t)
=\frac{\mathbf{r}'(t)}{||\mathbf{r}'(t)||}
= \frac{1}{\sqrt{36}}\langle 4,-4,2\rangle
=\left\langle \frac{4}{\sqrt{36}}, \frac{-4}{\sqrt{36}}, \frac{2}{\sqrt{36}} \right\rangle.</me>
We see that the unit tangent is constant, since the curve is a straight line.


</solution>
